{
  "reasons": {
    "detach": "`{command}` would detach HEAD in {repo}. Agents share that repository's working tree on one branch: moving HEAD there moves the files under every agent, and their next commits land wherever HEAD went. To work at another commit, make a clone of your own (`git clone --local --no-checkout {repo} <dir>`, then `git -C <dir> checkout -q <commit>`), or read a file with `git show <commit>:<path>`. If the owner wants this here, ask them to run it in their own terminal.",
    "branch": "`{command}` would create, reset, rename or copy branch `{target}` in {repo}. Agents share that repository's working tree on one branch: moving HEAD there moves the files under every agent, and their next commits land wherever HEAD went. Commit on the branch HEAD is on, or use a branch in a clone of your own (`git clone --local {repo} <dir>`). If the owner wants this branch, ask them to run the command in their own terminal.",
    "switch": "`{command}` would move {repo}'s HEAD to `{target}`. Agents share that repository's working tree on one branch: moving HEAD there moves the files under every agent, and their next commits land wherever HEAD went. Read a file at another revision with `git show <rev>:<path>`, or check it out in a clone of your own (`git clone --local --no-checkout {repo} <dir>`, then `git -C <dir> checkout -q <rev>`). If the owner wants this here, ask them to run it in their own terminal.",
    "worktree": "`{command}` would add a worktree to {repo}. Agents share that repository, and worktrees are disabled there (AGENTS.md), so git would create the worktree's branch and then fail. Work in a clone of your own instead (`git clone --local {repo} <dir>`).",
    "detached": "HEAD is detached now, and `git switch {shared}` puts it back on the branch agents share.",
    "unattached": "HEAD is detached now, and its reflog names no branch that still exists, so you may switch to any local branch."
  },
  "examplesNote": "Each example runs the hook in a fixture (test-destructive-git.js). These repositories have the worktrees marker: `shared` and `sibling` on `master`, `main` on `main`, `trunk` on `trunk` with `pull.rebase` and `rebase.autoStash` set, `direction` on `direction/x`, `detached` with HEAD detached after it left `main`, `rebasing` detached in a rebase that returns to `trunk` after HEAD left `feature`, and `unattached` detached with a reflog that names no branch left. `clone` is a clone of `shared` without the marker, `missing` is a directory that does not exist, and `unknown` sends no working directory. `save` means the hook saved and let the command run, `unplaced` that it could not tell which repository the command writes and said so, `pass` that it let the command run silently.",
